# jabs – Cursor Rules
# Single-file vanilla-JS bubble shooter. Zero dependencies.
# See GLOSSARY.md for terminology, agent.md for prose rules.

# ─── Architecture ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Single BubbleShooter class. All logic lives as instance methods.
- Zero dependencies. No npm, no framework, no CDN, no build tool.
- All app code lives in index.htm. New files allowed only for docs/, test/, .github/.

# ─── SSoT (Single Source of Truth) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
- Hex topology: getRowOffsetFlag(row). NEVER row % 2.
- Aim direction: resolveAim(targetX, targetY). NEVER Math.atan2 elsewhere for shots.
- Turn resolution: resolveTurn() at end of placeBubble(). NEVER in shootBubble().
- Grid mutation: only inside BubbleShooter methods. NEVER external.
- DOM updates: updateUI() only. NEVER direct textContent in gameplay methods.

# ─── State ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- All state as instance properties on BubbleShooter (this.*).
- No DOM-as-state, no window.* properties, no localStorage.
- delete grid[r][c] to remove. NEVER null, '', 0, false.
- this.rowOffsets[row] caches row offsets (0 or 1). Use getRowOffsetFlag(row).

# ─── Inputs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Pointer Events only: pointerdown, pointermove, pointerup, pointercancel.
- Pointer Capture for drag-to-aim on touch.
- Keyboard: ArrowLeft/Right for aim, Space/Enter to shoot, Escape to close overlay.
- All aim paths funnel through resolveAim().

# ─── Turn Sequence (mandatory) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
shootBubble: create activeBubble, rotate queue, shotsFired++. NOTHING else.
placeBubble: place or explode, then checkMatches → removeFloating → resolveTurn.
resolveTurn: checkWin → nextLevel? else addRow? else checkGameOver.

# ─── Power-Ups ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Toggle via button click.
- Charge consumed on ARM, not on shoot.
- aimAssistShots-- inside shootBubble() after firing.
- bombArmed attached to activeBubble.powerUp on fire.
- resetPowerUps() at game start, level up, restart, game over.
- Button.disabled + aria-label reflect remaining charges.

# ─── Rendering ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Canvas 2D API only. No Pixi/Three/Phaser.
- SVG <line> for trajectory, NOT canvas.
- gameLoop order: clearRect → updateActiveBubble → grid draw → active bubble draw → raf.
- deltaTime from rAF timestamp, capped at 100ms.
- Substep collision: steps = min(50, max(1, ceil(stepDistance / (radius*0.5)))).
- drawBubble() never mutates state. Zeichenbefehle only.

# ─── Conventions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- ES6+ class syntax. const > let > var (var forbidden).
- camelCase vars/methods, PascalCase classes.
- === / !==. NEVER == / !=.
- Early returns. No nested if-else.
- Template literals. NEVER + string concat.
- Optional chaining where useful.
- JSDoc on public methods: @param + @returns.

# ─── Magic Numbers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- Shots per row (5) → this.shotsPerRow.
- Columns (15) → this.fixedColumns.
- Initial rows (8) → this.initialRows.
- Free rows (10) → this.bottomFreeRows.
- Bubble speed (480) → constant or comment.
- Power-up charges (1) → this.maxPowerUpCharges.
- Angle limits → this.baseAngleLimit, this.aimAngleLimit.

# ─── Forbidden ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- ❌ any new dependency in package.json (only devDependencies for tests).
- ❌ global event listeners outside setupEventListeners().
- ❌ setInterval/setTimeout for game logic (only UI debouncing).
- ❌ CSS !important.
- ❌ innerHTML for dynamic content.
- ❌ new files for game code.
- ❌ row % 2 for topology or positioning.
- ❌ separate touch/mouse event paths.

# ─── Pre-commit checklist ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
- npm test passes (syntax + 6 smoke tests).
- No conflict markers in diff.
- Doku updates reference GLOSSARY.md terms consistently.